# Privacy Policy

## Introduction

Our privacy policy explains what information we collect through the Clinical Intelligence application and browser extension, how we use it, and what choices you have.

We built Clinical Intelligence as a clinical follow-up system for healthcare providers. The service is intended to support medical consultation workflows and ongoing patient follow-up.

By using our service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. The personal information we collect is used to provide and improve the service. We do not sell your information or use it for advertising.

## Information Collection and Use

To provide the Clinical Intelligence service, we may collect personally identifiable information including, but not limited to:

* Patient name
* Phone number
* Date of birth
* Gender
* Symptoms, diagnoses, and treatment information
* Follow-up responses

This information is stored securely and used exclusively to provide clinical follow-up, communication, and related functionality.

## Chrome Extension and EHR Data

Our Clinical Intelligence EHR Capture browser extension allows healthcare professionals to capture relevant clinical information from an EHR page for use within the Clinical Intelligence service.

The extension only accesses the active EHR page when the clinician explicitly initiates a capture. The clinician remains in control of when information is captured. The extension does not continuously monitor EHR pages or automatically capture information in the background.

Captured information may include clinical information displayed on the EHR page, such as patient details, consultation notes, symptoms, diagnoses, and treatment information. This information is transmitted to the Clinical Intelligence service for processing, including AI-assisted extraction and organization, and for providing clinical follow-up functionality.

The captured information is used only to provide the functionality of the Clinical Intelligence service and is not sold or used for advertising.

## WhatsApp Communication

We use the WhatsApp Cloud API to send follow-up messages to patients after a medical consultation.

These messages may include:

* Post-consultation health check-ins
* Follow-up reminders
* Clinical status questions

Patients may respond using interactive WhatsApp buttons or messages. These responses are stored in our system to support clinical tracking and patient care.

Patients only receive WhatsApp messages after a consultation with a healthcare provider and as part of follow-up care.

## Data Storage

Personal and medical data is securely stored using Supabase database infrastructure. We take appropriate security measures to protect data against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.

## Service Providers

We may use third-party companies and individuals to:

* Provide and maintain the service
* Process and store data
* Support AI-assisted processing
* Send WhatsApp messages via the WhatsApp Cloud API
* Monitor system performance

These providers process data on our behalf and are contractually or otherwise required to protect your data and are not permitted to use it for purposes unrelated to providing their services.

## Security

We value your trust in providing personal information and use commercially acceptable means to protect it. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted on this page and take effect immediately upon posting.

